From b4a9993450f636b314485a07969600cc2be831a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grearjake-star <228037169+grearjake-star@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:27:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(flash next cuda): keep a state at the last 2048-row
 boundary before a system block's end

A system block that changes only near its end (a date line, a memory section) prefilled whole again,
because the shared block's state is kept only at the second message's start. Flash Next now keeps
one more state there: the last multiple of TF_SYS_CHECKPOINT rows (default 2048, a prompt pass; 0
off) at least MIN_GAP before that start, so a 13.1K block resumes at 12288. It is one more stop of
snapshot_points, so it is kept, forked and evicted like the message-start state, within the same
kept-state count. Other families pass no granule and keep their points as before.

A resume restores a kept prefix, so the reply is a fresh prefill's, token for token.
